  <static seed="1914" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/NumberBasics/AbsoluteValue14.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \left\lvert{{\frac{43}{19}}}\right\rvert= }</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{43}{19}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The absolute value of <m>{{\frac{43}{19}}}</m> is the distance between <m>{{\frac{43}{19}}}</m> and <m>0</m> on the number line. In this case, since <m>{{\frac{43}{19}}}</m> is <m>{{\frac{43}{19}}}</m> units away from 0, the answer is <m>{{\frac{43}{19}}}</m>.</p>
</solution>
